  "findings": [
    "All four unmodified JA/EN examples correctly print168primes<=1000; no false claim of failure at the actual fixed limit.",
    "Prose says N elements but indexing0throughN requires N+1.",
    "Starting atp² skips smaller multiples with a previously processed prime factor, not every smaller number being already enumerated.",
    "2 itself is prime; only even integers greater than2 are composite.",
